REPOSITORY LICENSE INDEX

No single license applies to the complete contents of this repository. This
file identifies license scope; it does not replace, weaken, or broaden any
license or notice stored within a method directory.

1. TOP-LEVEL COMPILATION MATERIAL

The top-level README.md, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, .gitignore, .gitattributes,
and the original selection and arrangement of those top-level materials are
made available under the MIT License in LICENSES/ROOT-MIT.txt, to the extent
that those materials are copyrightable and controlled by the repository
contributors.

That MIT grant does NOT apply to anything under Methods/ and does not relicense
third-party material.

2. METHOD-SPECIFIC SCOPE

Methods/TSLDSeg/
  The primary TSLDSeg upstream license is MIT. The directory also contains
  identified SDSeg-derived material; the retained CreativeML Open RAIL-M text
  in Methods/TSLDSeg/LICENSES/SDSeg-CreativeML-Open-RAIL-M.txt applies where
  relevant. Consult LICENSE, LICENSES/, UPSTREAM.md, MODIFICATIONS.md, and
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in that directory.

Methods/SDSeg/
  CreativeML Open RAIL-M, together with the retained third-party notices and
  license texts. Consult the method's LICENSE, LICENSES/, UPSTREAM.md,
  MODIFICATIONS.md, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Methods/MedSegV1/
  MIT for the identified primary upstream work, with separately identified
  third-party MIT portions. Consult the method's LICENSE and LICENSES/.

Methods/LEAF/
  MIT for the identified primary upstream work. Identified third-party portions
  include MIT- and Apache-2.0-licensed material. Consult the method's LICENSE,
  LICENSES/, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Methods/EnsemDiff/
  MIT for the identified primary upstream work. Identified third-party portions
  include MIT- and Apache-2.0-licensed material. Consult the method's LICENSE,
  LICENSES/, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Methods/cDAL/
  Primarily the NVIDIA Source Code License-NC. Use is restricted to the
  non-commercial research/evaluation scope stated in that license. Additional
  portions carry their own retained terms, including the separately documented
  NVIDIA LSGM license and processor condition. Consult the method's LICENSE,
  LICENSES/, UPSTREAM.md, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. This component is not
  provided under an OSI-approved open-source license.

3. FILE-SPECIFIC TERMS

Where a source file or a nearer LICENSE, NOTICE, COPYING, SPDX identifier, or
copyright header specifies different or additional terms, that more specific
notice controls for that material. Preserve all applicable notices and comply
with all conditions, including attribution, modification-notice, use-field,
and non-commercial restrictions.

Combining the six method directories in one Git repository is an aggregation
for navigation and reproducibility. It does not merge their licenses or grant
rights to datasets, model weights, papers, trademarks, or other assets that are
not included here.

This index is provided for release organization and is not legal advice.
